<h3 id="specification-cost">The specification cost, named</h3>
<p>The checker guarantees that a Form is valid; it does not guarantee that it is the Form that was meant. In verified LLM-driven synthesis for concept design, invariant-only synthesis "reached verified designs quickly but often produced inconsistent designs across runs", which shows "that invariants alone underconstrain the design task"; scenario-guided synthesis recovered intended designs more consistently [B23, abstract]. In seL4 the abstract specification took about 4 person-months and the proof about 20 person-years (Klein et al. 2009, Section 2 below). A closed program world makes acceptance exact and search tractable. It moves the uncertainty of intent into <span set:html={m(R`\sigma(\iota)`)} />; it does not remove it. Falsifier RJ-F2 below makes that cost public and measurable.</p>

